1,1,2,2,2,1],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[4,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,4],[4,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,4],[4,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,4,4,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,4],[4,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,4,4,3,3,3,4,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,4],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"The grid has two kinds of content.\n\n**Bands.** The lower part holds full-width horizontal bands. Each band has a fill colour *F* in its interior and a different end colour *E* in the first and last columns:\n- Pair 1: fill 3 / end 4, fill 2 / end 5, fill 8 / end 3.\n- Pair 2: fill 2 / end 4, fill 4 / end 6.\n- Pair 3: fill 3 / end 1, fill 8 / end 6.\n\n**Shapes.** The free background area above the bands holds small shapes. A shape can be one colour (pair 1's 2×2 block of 8) or a ring with a differently coloured inside (pair 1's 3-ring around 2s).\n\n**What the outputs show.**\n- Every shape vanishes from the free area and becomes background.\n- Each colour part of a shape reappears inside the band whose fill colour equals that colour.\n- It is painted in that band's end colour.\n- It keeps its exact x-columns and its own silhouette.\n- It is cropped to the bounding box of that colour's own cells and pushed down so it touches the band's bottom row.\n- Band cells that the part does not cover keep the band's fill colour, so holes stay visible.\n\n**Checks against the demonstrations.**\n- Pair 1, the ring 3 around 2s at rows 2–4, x 7–12:\n  - The 3-cells land in the 3-band at rows 14–16 as colour 4.\n  - The inner 2s (one row, x 8–11) land on row 23, the bottom row of the 2-band, as colour 5.\n- Pair 1, the 2-ring with an 8 centre at x 2–4:\n  - The ring goes to the 2-band as 5.\n  - Its single 8 cell goes to row 28 of the 8-band, x 3, as colour 3.\n- Pair 1, the plain 8 block at x 17–18 goes to the bottom of the 8-band as colour 3.\n- Pair 3, the 8-shape with a background notch:\n  - It goes to rows 27–29 of the 8-band as colour 6.\n  - The notch shows as 8, the band's fill colour.\n- Pair 2: the 2-ring with two 4-blocks inside follows the same pattern. The ring lands in the 2-band as 4, and the blocks land at the bottom of the 4-band as 6.\n\n**Test.** The bands are fill 1 / end 3, fill 2 / end 1, and fill 3 / end 4. The shapes map as follows:\n- 1-ring with a 2 centre: ring goes to the 1-band as 3; the centre goes to the 2-band as 1.\n- 3 block: goes to the 3-band as 4.\n- 2-capsule with 3 inside: the capsule goes to the 2-band as 1; the 3s go to the 3-band as 4.\n\n**Program.**\n1. Detect band rows: interior constant at *F*, both end cells equal to *E*, and *E* ≠ *F*. Group consecutive rows that share the same (*F*, *E*).\n2. Clear every non-band, non-background cell to background.\n3. For each multicolour object, and for each colour inside it, bottom-align that colour's mask in the band with matching fill and paint it in the band's end colour.\n\nI emit one checkpoint after clearing the free area, then one after each object is stamped.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    # detect band rows\n    bandrow = {}\n    for y in range(H):\n        inner = g[y, 1:W-1]\n        if (inner == inner[0]).all() and g[y, 0] == g[y, W-1] and g[y, 0] != inner[0]:\n            bandrow[y] = (int(inner[0]), int(g[y, 0]))\n    # group into bands: fill -> (top, bottom, end)\n    bands = {}\n    for y in sorted(bandrow):\n        f, e = bandrow[y]\n        if f in bands and bands[f][1] == y - 1:\n            t, b, _ = bands[f]\n            bands[f] = (t, y, e)\n        else:\n            bands[f] = (y, y, e)\n    free = np.ones_like(g, dtype=bool)\n    for y in bandrow:\n        free[y, :] = False\n    sub = g.copy()\n    sub[~free] = bg\n    objs = objects(sub, bg=bg, multicolour=True)\n    out = g.copy()\n    out[free & (g != bg)] = bg\n    emit(out, \"Remove all shapes from the free area above the bands.\")\n    for o in objs:\n        cols = sorted(set(int(g[y, x]) for y, x in o[\"cells\"]))\n        for c in cols:\n            if c not in bands:\n                continue\n            cells = [(y, x) for y, x in o[\"cells\"] if g[y, x] == c]\n            y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(cells)\n            t, b, e = bands[c]\n            dy = b - y1\n            for y, x in cells:\n                ny = y + dy\n                if t <= ny <= b:\n                    out[ny, x] = e\n        emit(out, f\"Drop each colour part of the shape at {o['box']} to the bottom of its matching band, painted in the band's end colour.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each multicolour object, and for each colour inside it, bottom-align that colour's mask in the band with matching fill and paint it in the band's end colour."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I emit one checkpoint after clearing the free area, then one after each object is stamped."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each band has a fill colour *F* in its interior and a different end colour *E* in the first and last columns:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Band cells that the part does not cover keep the band's fill colour, so holes stay visible."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Detect band rows: interior constant at *F*, both end cells equal to *E*, and *E* ≠ *F*."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- It is cropped to the bounding box of that colour's own cells and pushed down so it touches the band's bottom row."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- It is cropped to the bounding box of that colour's own cells and pushed down so it touches the band's bottom row."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"f070735996888debd1e20b35f8138f90d7cf1afb8df81d264376c457de796362",